<section class="cxx entity method">

  <h1 id="Arcadia_ByteArray_createByteArray">Arcadia_ByteArray_createByteArray</h1>

  <my-signature><code>
  Arcadia_ByteArray*<br>
  Arcadia_ByteArray_createByteArray<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;(<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Arcadia_Thread* thread,<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Arcadia_RuntimeByteArray* runtimeByteArray<br>
  &nbsp;&nbsp;)
  </code></my-signature>

  <my-summary>Wraps an immutable runtime byte array in an object-level byte array.</my-summary>

  <section class="cxx parameters">
    <h1>Parameters</h1>
    <div>
      <div><code>Arcadia_Thread* thread</code></div>
      <div>A pointer to the calling thread.</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div><code>Arcadia_RuntimeByteArray* runtimeByteArray</code></div>
      <div>The immutable runtime byte array to wrap.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cxx return-value">
    <h1>Return value</h1>
    <p>An immutable, fixed-size and contiguous <code>Arcadia_ByteArray*</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="cxx remarks">
    <h1>Remarks</h1>
    <p>This compatibility function delegates to <code>Arcadia_ByteArrayFactory_createImmutable</code>. It does not copy the underlying bytes. The wrapper retains the runtime byte array through garbage-collector visitation.</p>
  </section>

</section>
